  "ssml": "<speak version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xmlns:mstts=\"https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" xml:lang=\"en-PH\">\n  <voice name=\"en-PH-RosaNeural\">\n    <mstts:express-as style=\"friendly\">\n      <prosody rate=\"95%\" pitch=\"+2%\">\n        Let&apos;s bring analogies home to Davao Oriental! <break time=\"550ms\"/> Tap the glowing pins on the island map above. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Up on Mount <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"hɑːmiˈɡiːtɑːn\">Hamiguitan</phoneme> in San Isidro, <break time=\"300ms\"/> the <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Philippine Eagle</emphasis> soars above ancient bonsai trees. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Down in <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"ˈmɑːti\">Mati</phoneme> City, <break time=\"300ms\"/> gentle dugongs and <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"pɑːˈwiːkɑːn\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">pawikan</emphasis></phoneme> swim in <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"puːˈhɑːdɑː\">Pujada</phoneme> Bay. <break time=\"550ms\"/> So we can say: Eagle is to Mount <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"hɑːmiˈɡiːtɑːn\">Hamiguitan</phoneme>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as dugong is to <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"puːˈhɑːdɑː\">Pujada</phoneme> Bay!\n      </prosody>\n    </mstts:express-as>\n  </voice>\n</speak>",
